@@ -22,6 +22,34 @@ The following table provides an outline of the features Trivy offers.
 These may be enabled or disabled depending on the target.
 See [here](./index.md) for the detail.
 
+## Liberica JDK and Liberica NIK
+Standalone installations of [BellSoft Liberica JDK](https://bell-sw.com/libericajdk/) —
+tarballs, `.deb`/`.rpm` packages, `COPY`ed runtimes in any image — are detected
+and scanned against the advisories BellSoft publishes for the product
+(OSV ecosystem `Liberica JDK:<major>`). Trivy anchors on the HotSpot library
+(`libjvm.so`, `libjvm.dylib`, `jvm.dll`), reads the vendor and the runtime
+version from its string table and corroborates them with the `release` file
+(`IMPLEMENTOR`, `JAVA_RUNTIME_VERSION`) or, for Java 8, the `rt.jar` manifest.
+Runtimes of other vendors (Azul, Eclipse Adoptium, Oracle, Amazon, ...) are
+ignored. A BellSoft runtime with GraalVM markers is Liberica Native Image Kit:
+it is reported once, as `liberica-nik` (ecosystem
+`Liberica NIK:<nik major>-<java major>`, package `core`, `standard` or `full`,
+version such as `23.1.0+1`), never as a JDK.
+
+The package name is the distribution variant (`jdk`, `jre`, `jdk-lite`,
+`jdk-full`, `jdk-crac`, ...), the version is the product version (`21.0.2+14`,
+`8u402+7`) and the purl is `pkg:generic/bellsoft/liberica-jdk@<version>?package_type=<variant>`.
+Runtimes installed by apk on Alpaquita Linux or BellSoft Hardened Containers
+(`/usr/lib/jvm/...`) are covered by the OS package scan and are not reported
+twice. The advisories come from the same OSV source as the
+[Alpaquita](../os/alpaquita.md#vulnerability) ones; by default the Liberica
+archives are fetched from `https://packages.bell-sw.com/osv`
+(`--vendor-url`, `--vendor-feed`).
+
+| Artifact     | SBOM | Vulnerability | License |
+|--------------|:----:|:-------------:|:-------:|
+| Liberica JDK |  ✓   |       ✓       |    -    |
+
 ## JAR/WAR/PAR/EAR
 To find information about your JAR[^2] file, Trivy parses `pom.properties` and `MANIFEST.MF` files in your JAR[^2] file and takes required properties[^3].
 Only the main section of `MANIFEST.MF` is used for artifact properties, because the individual sections that may follow it describe packages or files inside the archive rather than the archive itself.
